{
 "id": "01a0fcc7-df3a-7791-ba28-a6c717bc0412",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (since Finance switched accounting tools in late Sept 2026, per the user on 2026-10-02): plain comma-separated values (`,`) and ISO dates `YYYY-MM-DD` (strftime `%Y-%m-%d`). UTF-8 without a BOM. The previous tool's German-locale format (`;` delimiter, `DD.MM.YYYY` dates) is obsolete.",
 "premise": "while Finance uses the accounting tool they adopted in late September 2026"
}
